  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="813d-73c7-05ad-7345" name="Hittite Empire (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #113 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The Hittite kingdom centred on the uplands of Anatolia (modern Turkey) and grew to encompass most of Asia Minor and parts of Syria. Expansion into the latter area caused a long war with Egypt and the famous battle of Kadesh, a Hittite victory. The state finally succumbed to the Sea Peoples, although Neo- Hittite kingdoms survived to be conquered by Assyria. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Hittite Empire]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: at least 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Chariotry: at least 25% Infantry: At least 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
